.TH HOST-RESOLVE 1 "2026-10-13" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
host-resolve \- system host resolver forward and reverse checks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B host-resolve
.RB ( --name " HOST [" --family " any|ipv4|ipv6] | " --address " IP) [" --null ]
.br
.B host-resolve
.RB [ --help | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Use the host's getaddrinfo/getnameinfo interfaces. Results can come from
hosts files, caches, mDNS or DNS. Not a direct DNS protocol check.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --name " HOST"
Resolve a hostname to one or more numeric addresses.
.TP
.BI --address " IP"
Resolve numeric IPv4/IPv6 address to a hostname, without numeric fallback.
.TP
.BI --family " any|ipv4|ipv6"
Address family for forward resolution only. Default any.
.TP
.B --null
Emit four NUL-separated DIRECTION, FAMILY, ADDRESS, NAME fields per result.
.TP
.B --help
Display usage information.
.TP
.B --version
Display version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 resolved; 1 unsuccessful; 2 invalid options; 3 internal conversion failure.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Perl Socket with getaddrinfo/getnameinfo (typically Perl 5.14 or newer).
.SH SEE ALSO
getaddrinfo(3), getnameinfo(3), hosts(5)
